  "notes": "General Biotechnology option, University Park. Uses the standard CHEM 110/112/210/212/213 organic-chemistry path rather than the bulletin's alternate CHEM 202/203 sequence, matching every other Eberly Science major's modeling. 'Department List C' electives (14 credits total) are modeled generically, same convention as BIOL's 'Supporting Course' slots. 'etm' marks the gateway courses (Chem I, Calc I, BMB 251) everything downstream depends on. Post-prereq-parser-fix repair: CHEM 110's real prereq is MATH 22, which was never in this plan -- and MATH 22 itself real-chains through MATH 21, MATH 4, and MATH 3, none of which were present either, leaving CHEM 110 (and everything after it, including MICRB 201/BMB 251/BMB 252) permanently unschedulable. Added MATH 3/MATH 4 (Semester 1) and MATH 21/MATH 22 (Semester 2) explicitly to complete the real chain. FLAGGED FOR HUMAN REVIEW: even with this real, catalog-confirmed fix, the plan no longer completes in 4 years (8 terms) -- it needs 9. The MATH 3->4->21->22 chain (4 sequential terms, unavoidable: none of these have concurrent_groups) pushes CHEM 110 to term 5, and BIOTECH's own critical path needs 5 more sequential terms after that (CHEM 110 -> CHEM 112 -> BMB 251 -> BMB 252 -> BIOTC 459/479/MICRB 410), for a genuine structural minimum of 9 terms. This isn't a credit-capacity issue (raising max_credits_per_semester does not help; several simulated terms land well under the existing 17cr cap) -- it's the length of the real prereq chain itself. Verified clean (no warnings, goal met) at grad_years=5 (9 terms). Not patched further here since doing so would require either dropping a real requirement or inventing a substitute path not supported by the actual catalog data.",
